  42:     - The first row is complete: it shows the diagonal color, the previous cycle color, then paired runs of the palette cycle.
  43:     - Every non-black input pixel already agrees with the hidden table.
  44: 
  45:     Rule:
  46:     - Read the palette cycle from every other first-row cell starting at column 2, stopping when the diagonal color repeats.
  47:     - For a cell, let near = min(row, column) and dist = abs(row - column).
  48:     - Use the diagonal color when dist is 0, the previous cycle color when dist <= near + 1, otherwise cycle through blocks of width near + 2.
  49: 
  50:     Key insight:
